1
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:02,420
Take a matrix.

2
00:00:02,700 --> 00:00:04,410
Two rows, two columns.

3
00:00:04,710 --> 00:00:05,530
Four numbers.

4
00:00:06,320 --> 00:00:08,400
At some point, someone told you to

5
00:00:08,640 --> 00:00:10,690
multiply them in a cross, and subtract.

6
00:00:11,250 --> 00:00:13,620
A times D, minus B times C.

7
00:00:13,950 --> 00:00:16,120
They called the answer the determinant.

8
00:00:16,910 --> 00:00:18,690
And you probably learned to compute it,

9
00:00:18,910 --> 00:00:21,060
long before anyone told you what it is.

10
00:00:21,910 --> 00:00:23,780
You would think it is just a recipe.

11
00:00:24,050 --> 00:00:25,060
A piece of bookkeeping.

12
00:00:25,630 --> 00:00:26,170
But watch.

13
00:00:26,960 --> 00:00:29,660
This one number knows how much a matrix

14
00:00:29,740 --> 00:00:30,830
stretches space.

15
00:00:31,060 --> 00:00:32,860
It knows whether space has been flipped

16
00:00:33,020 --> 00:00:33,200
over.

17
00:00:33,450 --> 00:00:35,580
And when it reaches zero, it is telling

18
00:00:35,660 --> 00:00:37,660
you that something has been destroyed, and

19
00:00:37,740 --> 00:00:38,840
can never be recovered.

20
00:00:40,130 --> 00:00:42,000
By the end of this video, you will look at

21
00:00:42,080 --> 00:00:44,640
A times D, minus B times C, and see a

22
00:00:44,720 --> 00:00:46,190
picture instead of a formula.

23
00:00:47,080 --> 00:00:49,260
We will start with a single square, and

24
00:00:49,460 --> 00:00:51,890
end by flattening three dimensional space.

25
00:00:58,050 --> 00:01:00,510
First, we need to see what a matrix does.

26
00:01:01,480 --> 00:01:03,710
Start with a flat grid, and two arrows.

27
00:01:04,100 --> 00:01:06,040
One points to the right, one unit long.

28
00:01:06,370 --> 00:01:07,230
Call it i hat.

29
00:01:07,580 --> 00:01:09,220
The other points straight up.

30
00:01:09,490 --> 00:01:10,280
Call it j hat.

31
00:01:11,190 --> 00:01:13,400
A matrix is a set of instructions for

32
00:01:13,480 --> 00:01:14,650
moving this whole grid.

33
00:01:14,940 --> 00:01:16,760
And the instructions are surprisingly

34
00:01:17,450 --> 00:01:17,720
short.

35
00:01:17,720 --> 00:01:19,740
The first column says where i hat lands.

36
00:01:20,060 --> 00:01:22,170
The second column says where j hat lands.

37
00:01:23,170 --> 00:01:24,170
Take this matrix.

38
00:01:24,530 --> 00:01:26,460
Its first column is three, one.

39
00:01:26,680 --> 00:01:30,007
So i hat moves to the point three, one.

40
00:01:30,007 --> 00:01:31,690
Its second column is one, two.

41
00:01:31,910 --> 00:01:33,160
So j hat goes there.

42
00:01:33,930 --> 00:01:35,740
And everything else follows along.

43
00:01:36,250 --> 00:01:37,390
Grid lines stay straight.

44
00:01:37,690 --> 00:01:40,293
They stay parallel, and evenly spaced.

45
00:01:40,347 --> 00:01:42,760
The whole plane leans and stretches,

46
00:01:42,800 --> 00:01:44,210
carried by those two arrows.

47
00:01:45,130 --> 00:01:46,970
That is all a matrix is.

48
00:01:47,270 --> 00:01:48,590
A movement of space.

49
00:01:49,090 --> 00:01:51,060
And once you see it that way, a natural

50
00:01:51,220 --> 00:01:51,920
question appears.

51
00:01:52,260 --> 00:01:54,010
How much did space just stretch?

52
00:01:56,040 --> 00:01:58,080
To measure it, watch one small piece of

53
00:01:58,120 --> 00:01:58,500
the grid.

54
00:01:58,740 --> 00:02:01,600
The square that sits on i hat and j hat.

55
00:02:01,600 --> 00:02:03,920
Each side has length one, so its area is

56
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:04,740
exactly one.

57
00:02:05,570 --> 00:02:07,290
Now apply the matrix again.

58
00:02:07,600 --> 00:02:09,513
The square leans over into a

59
00:02:09,647 --> 00:02:10,140
parallelogram.

60
00:02:10,510 --> 00:02:12,610
Count it up, and its area is five.

61
00:02:13,470 --> 00:02:14,990
One became five.

62
00:02:15,470 --> 00:02:17,060
And here is what makes this useful.

63
00:02:17,390 --> 00:02:18,930
It is not just that square.

64
00:02:19,340 --> 00:02:21,080
Every square on the grid was treated the

65
00:02:21,200 --> 00:02:23,640
same way, so every one of them grew five

66
00:02:23,720 --> 00:02:24,420
times larger.

67
00:02:25,240 --> 00:02:28,260
And any shape you like, a circle, a leaf,

68
00:02:28,300 --> 00:02:30,220
the outline of a country, can be filled

69
00:02:30,300 --> 00:02:31,410
with tiny squares.

70
00:02:31,610 --> 00:02:33,790
Each tiny square grows by five.

71
00:02:34,060 --> 00:02:35,680
So the whole shape grows by five.

72
00:02:36,650 --> 00:02:39,040
That factor, the amount by which a matrix

73
00:02:39,120 --> 00:02:41,430
scales every area, is the determinant.

74
00:02:41,710 --> 00:02:44,200
For this matrix, the determinant is five.

75
00:02:45,170 --> 00:02:46,240
Let us test the idea.

76
00:02:46,660 --> 00:02:48,660
This matrix stretches space by two

77
00:02:48,740 --> 00:02:50,460
sideways, and by three upward.

78
00:02:50,850 --> 00:02:53,180
A one by one square becomes two by three.

79
00:02:53,520 --> 00:02:54,900
The determinant is six.

80
00:02:55,800 --> 00:02:57,320
Now try to predict this one.

81
00:02:57,650 --> 00:02:59,050
It is called a shear.

82
00:02:59,550 --> 00:03:01,560
The top of the grid slides to the right,

83
00:03:01,640 --> 00:03:02,820
while the bottom stays put.

84
00:03:03,420 --> 00:03:04,690
Everything looks distorted.

85
00:03:05,160 --> 00:03:06,530
So what is the determinant?

86
00:03:07,610 --> 00:03:08,240
It is one.

87
00:03:08,700 --> 00:03:10,780
The square leans, but its base and its

88
00:03:10,860 --> 00:03:12,080
height never change.

89
00:03:12,490 --> 00:03:14,700
Shapes are bent, and yet not a drop of

90
00:03:14,780 --> 00:03:16,430
area is gained or lost.

91
00:03:18,260 --> 00:03:20,120
So where does the formula come from?

92
00:03:20,460 --> 00:03:22,980
Why A times D, minus B times C?

93
00:03:23,900 --> 00:03:25,310
Write the matrix with letters.

94
00:03:25,660 --> 00:03:27,450
i hat lands at A, C.

95
00:03:27,890 --> 00:03:29,710
j hat lands at B, D.

96
00:03:29,940 --> 00:03:31,980
And the parallelogram between them is the

97
00:03:32,140 --> 00:03:32,730
area we want.

98
00:03:33,610 --> 00:03:34,930
Here is a lovely trick.

99
00:03:35,280 --> 00:03:37,150
Draw a rectangle around the whole thing.

100
00:03:37,570 --> 00:03:39,110
Its width is A plus B.

101
00:03:39,460 --> 00:03:41,030
Its height is C plus D.

102
00:03:41,950 --> 00:03:43,550
That rectangle is too big.

103
00:03:43,910 --> 00:03:45,510
So remove what does not belong.

104
00:03:45,880 --> 00:03:48,260
Two triangles here, which together make A

105
00:03:48,420 --> 00:03:48,900
times C.

106
00:03:49,350 --> 00:03:51,650
Two more triangles, which make B times D.

107
00:03:51,860 --> 00:03:54,000
And two small rectangles in the corners,

108
00:03:54,250 --> 00:03:55,790
each one B times C.

109
00:03:56,620 --> 00:03:59,000
Expand, subtract, and almost everything

110
00:03:59,080 --> 00:03:59,600
cancels.

111
00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:02,760
What survives is A times D, minus B times

112
00:04:02,920 --> 00:04:03,180
C.

113
00:04:04,010 --> 00:04:05,950
So the formula was never arbitrary.

114
00:04:06,250 --> 00:04:08,460
It is the area of a parallelogram, written

115
00:04:08,540 --> 00:04:09,730
out in four numbers.

116
00:04:10,570 --> 00:04:11,790
Try it on our matrix.

117
00:04:12,160 --> 00:04:13,710
Three times two is six.

118
00:04:14,040 --> 00:04:15,440
One times one is one.

119
00:04:15,770 --> 00:04:16,840
Six minus one.

120
00:04:17,250 --> 00:04:17,670
Five.

121
00:04:18,050 --> 00:04:19,360
The same five we counted.

122
00:04:21,240 --> 00:04:23,410
But a subtraction can fall below zero.

123
00:04:23,620 --> 00:04:25,260
And an area cannot be negative.

124
00:04:25,730 --> 00:04:27,660
So what would a determinant of negative

125
00:04:27,820 --> 00:04:28,260
five mean?

126
00:04:29,120 --> 00:04:31,470
Take our matrix, and swap its two columns.

127
00:04:31,790 --> 00:04:34,720
Now i hat lands where j hat used to, and j

128
00:04:34,840 --> 00:04:36,220
hat lands where i hat was.

129
00:04:36,630 --> 00:04:38,640
The parallelogram is the same shape.

130
00:04:38,720 --> 00:04:39,550
The same area.

131
00:04:39,770 --> 00:04:41,860
But the formula gives negative five.

132
00:04:42,700 --> 00:04:43,560
Look at the arrows.

133
00:04:43,900 --> 00:04:46,180
On the original grid, j hat sits to the

134
00:04:46,260 --> 00:04:47,110
left of i hat.

135
00:04:47,560 --> 00:04:49,560
After this matrix, it sits to the right.

136
00:04:50,050 --> 00:04:52,100
Space has been turned over, like a sheet

137
00:04:52,180 --> 00:04:53,760
of paper flipped onto its back.

138
00:04:54,170 --> 00:04:56,100
Any writing on it now reads in mirror

139
00:04:56,180 --> 00:04:56,600
image.

140
00:04:57,410 --> 00:04:59,070
That is what the sign records.

141
00:04:59,320 --> 00:05:01,320
The size of the determinant is how much

142
00:05:01,400 --> 00:05:02,260
area scales.

143
00:05:02,520 --> 00:05:04,200
The sign tells you whether space was

144
00:05:04,280 --> 00:05:04,630
flipped.

145
00:05:05,410 --> 00:05:07,050
And you can watch the sign change.

146
00:05:07,360 --> 00:05:09,570
Swing j hat slowly toward i hat.

147
00:05:10,030 --> 00:05:11,740
The parallelogram gets thinner, and the

148
00:05:11,780 --> 00:05:12,850
determinant falls.

149
00:05:13,130 --> 00:05:15,420
Then the two arrows line up, and for one

150
00:05:15,500 --> 00:05:17,190
instant, it is exactly zero.

151
00:05:17,610 --> 00:05:19,260
Keep going, and it comes out the other

152
00:05:19,290 --> 00:05:20,410
side, negative.

153
00:05:21,210 --> 00:05:23,270
Zero is the doorway between the two.

154
00:05:23,550 --> 00:05:25,640
And zero is the most important value a

155
00:05:25,680 --> 00:05:26,700
determinant can take.

156
00:05:28,490 --> 00:05:30,300
When the determinant is zero, the two

157
00:05:30,380 --> 00:05:32,220
arrows land on the same line.

158
00:05:32,300 --> 00:05:34,167
And everything else goes with them.

159
00:05:34,167 --> 00:05:36,140
The whole plane is squashed onto that

160
00:05:36,220 --> 00:05:36,500
line.

161
00:05:37,360 --> 00:05:39,280
Every shape now has zero area.

162
00:05:39,620 --> 00:05:41,050
But something worse has happened.

163
00:05:41,390 --> 00:05:42,300
Look at these points.

164
00:05:42,640 --> 00:05:44,290
They started in different places.

165
00:05:44,640 --> 00:05:46,350
Now they sit on top of each other.

166
00:05:47,160 --> 00:05:48,820
So suppose I show you where a point

167
00:05:48,900 --> 00:05:51,010
landed, and ask you where it came from.

168
00:05:51,570 --> 00:05:52,640
You cannot tell me.

169
00:05:52,990 --> 00:05:55,460
A whole line of starting points all ended

170
00:05:55,540 --> 00:05:55,910
up there.

171
00:05:56,440 --> 00:05:58,040
The information is gone.

172
00:05:59,110 --> 00:06:01,560
That is why a matrix with determinant zero

173
00:06:01,800 --> 00:06:03,040
has no inverse.

174
00:06:03,470 --> 00:06:04,900
There is no way to undo it.

175
00:06:05,220 --> 00:06:07,640
You cannot unsquash a line back into a

176
00:06:07,720 --> 00:06:08,070
plane.

177
00:06:09,100 --> 00:06:11,100
And it is why this is the first thing to

178
00:06:11,180 --> 00:06:12,460
check when you solve a system of

179
00:06:12,540 --> 00:06:13,190
equations.

180
00:06:13,470 --> 00:06:16,380
A nonzero determinant means exactly one

181
00:06:16,580 --> 00:06:16,830
answer.

182
00:06:17,020 --> 00:06:19,660
A determinant of zero means the answer is

183
00:06:19,780 --> 00:06:21,980
either missing, or there are infinitely

184
00:06:21,980 --> 00:06:22,290
many.

185
00:06:24,310 --> 00:06:26,200
Everything we have said survives the move

186
00:06:26,280 --> 00:06:27,350
into three dimensions.

187
00:06:27,710 --> 00:06:30,080
Only one word changes.

188
00:06:30,080 --> 00:06:32,440
Now there are three arrows, and a three by

189
00:06:32,520 --> 00:06:34,700
three matrix tells each one where to land.

190
00:06:35,340 --> 00:06:37,800
Instead of a unit square, follow a unit

191
00:06:37,880 --> 00:06:38,230
cube.

192
00:06:38,640 --> 00:06:41,293
It is carried into a slanted box.

193
00:06:41,293 --> 00:06:43,440
The determinant is the volume of that box.

194
00:06:43,650 --> 00:06:45,560
The factor by which every volume is

195
00:06:45,570 --> 00:06:46,020
scaled.

196
00:06:47,030 --> 00:06:49,580
The sign still means a flip.

197
00:06:49,580 --> 00:06:51,860
Space is turned into its own mirror image,

198
00:06:51,900 --> 00:06:53,620
and a right hand becomes a left hand.

199
00:06:54,680 --> 00:06:56,670
And zero still means collapse.

200
00:06:57,120 --> 00:06:59,830
All of space pressed flat, onto a plane.

201
00:07:00,140 --> 00:07:01,160
Volume zero.

202
00:07:01,480 --> 00:07:03,510
And once again, no way back.

203
00:07:05,430 --> 00:07:06,550
Now for the payoff.

204
00:07:06,810 --> 00:07:08,330
There is a rule you may have met.

205
00:07:08,820 --> 00:07:10,780
The determinant of a product, is the

206
00:07:10,980 --> 00:07:12,200
product of the determinants.

207
00:07:12,480 --> 00:07:14,540
Prove it with algebra, and you will fill a

208
00:07:14,540 --> 00:07:14,990
page.

209
00:07:15,800 --> 00:07:18,097
But look at it as a picture.

210
00:07:18,160 --> 00:07:20,570
Apply one matrix, and areas grow by five.

211
00:07:20,970 --> 00:07:23,440
Apply another, and they grow by two.

212
00:07:23,440 --> 00:07:25,760
Do both, one after the other, and areas

213
00:07:25,840 --> 00:07:26,930
have grown by ten.

214
00:07:27,450 --> 00:07:28,290
Of course they have.

215
00:07:28,660 --> 00:07:30,010
There is nothing left to prove.

216
00:07:31,980 --> 00:07:33,570
So let us gather what we found.

217
00:07:34,660 --> 00:07:36,300
A matrix moves space.

218
00:07:36,580 --> 00:07:38,640
The determinant measures how much that

219
00:07:38,720 --> 00:07:39,950
movement scales area.

220
00:07:40,230 --> 00:07:42,797
Or in three dimensions, volume.

221
00:07:43,380 --> 00:07:45,060
Its sign tells you whether space was

222
00:07:45,100 --> 00:07:45,450
flipped.

223
00:07:46,170 --> 00:07:49,107
And when it is zero, space has collapsed,

224
00:07:49,133 --> 00:07:50,870
and the matrix cannot be undone.

225
00:07:51,800 --> 00:07:54,100
A times D, minus B times C.

226
00:07:54,530 --> 00:07:55,760
It was never a recipe.

227
00:07:56,200 --> 00:07:58,100
It is the area of a parallelogram.

228
00:07:58,490 --> 00:08:00,700
And now, you can see it.
